comment.narrative:
1.	A total of 699 (M 534 F 165) and 87 extension agents (M 69 F 18) have been able to share experiences and innovations between universities and research institutions as well as relevant line institutions through the organized Woreda level Forum meetings;
2. total of 50 (male 37, and 13 female) shared knowledge and skill through organized study tour on participatory forest management, agroforestry practices, and restoration of degraded lands.
3. A total of 373 (236 M 137 F) farmers and 87 extension agents 42 (34 M 8 F) participated in the knowledge sharing forum meetings organized Inter-Regional Forum meeting;
4. A total of 350,541 (173,864 M and 176,677 F) beneficiaries have become aware of implementing appropriate watershed management practices including SWC management and afforestation practices;
5. A total of 318,589 (162,694 M & 155,895 F) beneficiaries received Information on 3 seasonal and 48 decadal meteorological information to early warn farmers. The beneficiaries farming communities used the information and agrometeorological advisory service during their farming practice
6. A total of 1175 (M 764 and F 411) beneficiary farmers were demonstrated on learning by doing programs that helps the farmers as examples in six agricultural demonstration sites.
7. A total of 2,750,015 seedlings (tree and fruits) have been produced within the CCA project nurseries across the project Woredas. 
8. A total of 1,065.9 -hectare of degraded watershed areas have been covered by planting trees. 
9. A total 1875 (of which 1218 Female) received inputs such as drought resistance crop and market demanding vegetable seeds to enable them to undertake CSA practices as well as their capacity were enhanced through the provision of regular technical support.
